ged when director rob  reiner found love  he was dealing with some heavy personal  issues while making the film and as he  explained to people tv in 2018 i was  single for 10 years and making a mess of  my personal life in and out of  relationships and not being able to make  anything work but then while shooting  the film reiner met the woman who would  become his wife michelle singer  that radically altered his outlook on  everything including the ending of when  harry met sally caught in the swells of  romance reiner changed the finale during  the film thereby allowing harry and  sally to wind up together because when  you realize you want to spend the rest  of your life with somebody you want the  rest of your life to start as soon as  possible  while the name rambo has become  virtually synonymous with action movie  heroes from the 80s sylvester stallone's  one man army was nearly brought to a  definitive end in his debut film 1982's  first blood followed the vietnam war  veteran as he was targeted by an  overbearing small town sheriff leading  to an escalating conflict that saw rambo  outmaneuver the national guard and elude  authorities this showdown culminated  with rambo using a machine gun to shoot  up buildings throughout town before  being confronted by his old commanding  officer colonel troutman the original  ending mirrored the novel by david  morrell in which troutman shoots rambo  dead though in the film it's rambo who  manually forces his old friend to pull  the trigger effectively killing himself  though this ending was filmed and  included as a deleted scene on the home  video release director ted kochef told  entertainment weekly in 2017 that both  he and stallone felt the original  conclusion was too grim then they  conceived a new ending with rambo  surrendering to troutman  one of the most heartbreaking scenes in  star trek history is the death of mr  spock at the end of 1982's star trek ii  the wrath of khan in the film's climax  spock heroi