ive the t-rex the big moment instead  after being impressed by just how  powerful the creature's depiction became  during production  titanic was a phenomenal box office  success but it was also a major change  of pace for director james cameron as he  eschewed his penchant for action in  favor of a tragic period peace romance  the plot is framed by a treasure hunter  named brock lovett who explores the  wreckage of the title ship with one of  the few surviving passengers rose  calvert  rose recounts a whirlwind love story she  had before the ill-fated ocean liner  sank  after recalling her experience rose  drops the priceless diamond that brock  was searching for into the ocean leaving  him unaware that she had it the whole  time cameron had originally written and  filmed an ending scene in which rose's  granddaughter lizzie and brock witnessed  rose disposing of the diamond as a way  to resolve the fortune seeker's  character arc in this alternate version  rose allows brock to hold the diamond  before tossing it into the ocean as he  admits the treasure doesn't matter in  the grand scheme of life but cameron  ultimately felt the audience wouldn't be  invested in brock's character arc  following the extended flashback and  bill paxton who played brock agreed with  the decision  three years  i've thought of nothing except titanic  but i never got it  steven spielberg returned to the  blockbuster world of dinosaurs with the  1997 sequel the lost world jurassic park  the movie features the nefarious injen  corporation deciding to take dinosaurs  from isla sorna to a planned theme park  in california the survivors of this  expedition narrowly escape isla sorna  with their lives but then they must  contend with the t-rex rampaging through  the streets of san diego upon their  return this version of the finale was  suggested by spielberg five weeks before  the start of principal photography which  necessitated a rewrite from the original  ending  the original conclusion 